{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 3, :comments ["<b>And for his sister, a virgin.</b> The Sages said: 'his sister' — yes, he does not become impure, but he does become impure for a met mitzvah. And it is found in the book of the Rambam, z\"l, that this means a corpse lying on the road, and it is so distant from people that if the one who finds it calls out from that place, his voice would not be heard to others. And this is what the Sages call 'and there is no one after him to answer him' — this is a met mitzvah. And this is a great stringency, for it implies that if we find any people attending to it after him, the priest cannot become impure for a met mitzvah."], :book :leviticus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:08:20.330251399Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}